Declare a static wait queue head with DECLARE_WAIT_QUEUE_HEAD. The thread
function loops while !kthread_should_stop(), doing work and then sleeping with
wait_event_interruptible_timeout. The condition is kthread_should_stop() so the
thread wakes immediately when asked to stop. Use get_random_u32() % range for
jitter and msecs_to_jiffies() to convert milliseconds to jiffies.
